-- Rename every `viryaos_*` object to its unprefixed name: the schema predates the
-- CrowdRelay product name and the band's name ended up baked into platform
-- identifiers. `viryaos_autopilot_actions` becomes `autopilot_actions`, matching
-- the dominant convention (`community_posts`, `fan_*`, `workspaces` are already
-- unprefixed).
--
-- Generated from the live pg_catalog by scripts/gen_rename_viryaos.sql — do not
-- hand-edit; regenerate if earlier migrations change the catalog.
--
-- Coverage: 2431 constraints, 66 triggers, 133 tables, 23 sequences, 395
-- indexes, 2 views, 13 functions (rename + CREATE OR REPLACE, since RENAME does
-- not rewrite stored SQL bodies), plus `viryaos_*` compat views over every
-- renamed relation so binaries/agents from the previous release keep working
-- during the swap window. Drop the views in a follow-up migration once all
-- consumers run the new names.
--
-- Statements run in dependency order inside one transaction: constraints and
-- triggers reference their table by its old name, so they precede the table
-- renames; compat views come last, after every old name is released.

